Hydrogen gas reacts with molecular iodine in the gaseous state to produce hydroiodic acid, a  strong, colorless, corrosive gas with acidic properties. Suppose that a mixture made of 0.1moles of \ce{H2}, 0.3moles of \ce{I2}, and 0.01moles of \ce{HI} is placed in a 0.5L flask. Given the equilibrium constant for the reaction at a given temperature

\begin{center}\ce{H2_{(g)} + I2_{(g)}  <=> 2HI_{(g)}    }\hfill $K_c =100$\end{center}

calculate the equilibrium concentration of all species.
 \\
